WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.120
- So if you get a bug bite
on the train it could be

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:04.510
a little mosquito bite or
a near death experience.

00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:05.343
Happy Riding!

00:00:05.343 --> 00:00:08.420
(instrumental music)

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:12.790
- So I take the bus to
work every single day

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:15.390
and a couple weeks ago it rained in LA.

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:17.060
Which is a rare event here.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:19.610
And I got on the bus, it was pretty empty.

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:21.730
I picked a seat towards the back

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:24.270
and a few minutes in I notice a smell.

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:26.180
It's not a good smell.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:27.150
And I start to look around.

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:29.710
There are only about two
other people there with me

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:31.650
and it's not coming from either of them.

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:33.080
I'm not sure where it's coming.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:35.790
So I sit for a few seconds
thinking about this

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:39.720
and then I notice my butt is wet.

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:45.370
So I stand up kind of in shock
and try to convince myself

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:47.350
that it's just rain water.

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:48.680
That wasn't rain water.

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:50.620
It was definitely pee.

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:52.970
I was sitting in a strangers pee.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:55.530
On the bus.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:57.690
Turning around is not
an option at this point.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.770
It's gonna take like
an hour to get to work.

00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:03.020
The only thing I can do is go to Target

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:05.610
that's close to work and get pants.

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:08.800
So I went to Target and got
new pants, new underwear,

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:11.020
baby wipes, and a bottle of whiskey.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:14.720
Just to console myself because
it was eight o'clock in

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:16.860
the morning and this is
no way to start your day.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:19.410
It was the longest commute of my life.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:22.490
- I was on the bus going
back to my dad's house

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:24.940
with my two sisters in San Francisco.

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:27.960
My two sisters got off the bus
when we made it to the stop

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:30.680
but then I got like caught
behind for some reason

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:34.310
and this man just enters
the bus and he's like

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:37.170
shaking and like kind of falling over.

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:40.580
He's clearly drunk and
he's really really smelly.

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:42.180
Like I got a big whiff of him.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:45.160
He's coming close to me and
he's still falling over.

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:47.340
And he just goes like (blop).

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:50.080
He just like smears his hand on my face

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:53.210
like if I was a pole or
something to hold on to.

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:55.820
Holds it for like three, four seconds

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:57.670
and just walks right by.

00:01:57.670 --> 00:01:59.910
Unfazed, completely unfazed.

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:00.823
And I was just like.

00:02:00.823 --> 00:02:02.570
(horror music)

00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:06.270
I got off the bus and I started
screaming at my sisters.

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:08.190
I was like gimme the keys to the house.

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:09.670
Gimme the keys to the house.

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:11.900
My sisters were cracking up.

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:13.340
They thought it was the
most hilarious thing

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:15.050
because I am a huge germaphobe.

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:18.990
I went into the bathroom and
I took the rubbing alcohol

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:21.650
and I rubbed it all over my face.

00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:24.590
And then I went to grab the
dish soap because hand soap

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:26.330
is not gonna clean my face enough.

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:28.680
Took the dish soap and I washed my face

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:30.420
with it like two times.

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:33.770
If a drunk man is coming
on the bus and you see

00:02:33.770 --> 00:02:34.810
he's coming towards your way.

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:35.643
Run!

00:02:35.643 --> 00:02:38.360
Because he might use your
face to stabilize himself.

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:41.850
- I went up to San Francisco
to visit one of my best friends

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:43.930
and we were going to the ferry building

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.860
and we decided to take
the bus to get there.

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:49.850
But before we got on the
bus, we had a few mimosas.

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:52.530
So I was like a little
tipsy on this bus ride.

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:56.200
And we were standing up holding
on to the little rope thing

00:02:56.200 --> 00:03:00.090
you hold on to and I had this
little purse over my shoulder.

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:01.540
Wasn't really paying much attention.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:05.130
Then like two stops later
a ton of people got off

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:08.080
and after all this huge rush
of people got off this woman

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:10.180
who had been sitting down
kind of near where we were

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:13.810
standing was like "Oh, excuse
me ma'am, I think someone

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:15.380
"might have taken your
wallet out of your purse."

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:16.640
And she said it so calmly

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:18.990
that I almost didn't really believe her.

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:20.400
I was like, "what"?

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.490
And then sure enough I
like look in my purse

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:24.560
and my wallet is not in there anymore.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:27.960
And she's like "That guy that's
like just getting off, like

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:29.750
"about to walk off the
bus took your wallet."

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:32.420
And normally like soberly I think

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:33.480
I would have just been like

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:35.760
"Well shit, what do I do I guess

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:37.180
"I don't have my wallet anymore",

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:38.580
but because I was a little tipsy

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:39.970
and had this liquid courage,

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:42.430
I just walked right off
the bus and followed

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:45.030
this guy and I was like
"Hey! You stole my wallet!

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:46.140
"Give it back to me!"

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:48.280
And he's like "No I didn't, no I didn't,

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:49.113
"what are you talking about?"

00:03:49.113 --> 00:03:50.740
And then he just dropped my wallet

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:53.177
on the ground and like ran away.

00:03:53.177 --> 00:03:55.840
It was so weird but I just
like picked up my wallet

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:58.570
and all of the people on the
bus had totally been watching

00:03:58.570 --> 00:03:59.770
this whole thing go down.

00:03:59.770 --> 00:04:01.850
So when I got back on the bus
they were all like "Yeah!"

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:04.930
Like cheering for me that
I got my wallet back.

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:05.830
And then it was so weird.

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:07.950
We just kinda went on our way and it

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:10.260
was sort of like nothing happened.

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:12.700
- So it's the summer after
my junior year of college.

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:15.300
I'm using public transportation
every day for the first time

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:17.900
and I'm sitting there per the usual.

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:19.330
I don't like to get in anyone's way,

00:04:19.330 --> 00:04:22.240
so I like tuck in my
feet under the benches.

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:23.380
Great idea.

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:26.290
And I feel something tickle
my ankle and I look down

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:27.700
and I see like a mosquito flying away.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.470
I'm like "Oh great, I
got a mosquito bite."

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:31.870
For the next couple of
days I don't feel too well

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:32.860
but I didn't overthink it.

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:36.100
Suddenly on the second
night as I'm going to bed

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:37.730
I put my phone on my nightstand.

00:04:37.730 --> 00:04:40.790
And right before I put my
phone down I have lock jaw

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:42.850
and then I start shaking violently.

00:04:42.850 --> 00:04:45.060
And then next thing I know,
I'm projectile vomiting

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:47.470
into the trash can, on
my walls, everywhere.

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:48.630
And I pass out.

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:50.880
The next thing I know, I wake
up to my 4:00 a.m. alarm.

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:52.870
I go to work, I don't overthink it because

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:54.460
for some reason I feel good again.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:56.680
So I go to my boss casually
tell him "I'm not feeling too

00:04:56.680 --> 00:04:58.490
"well, maybe it's because
of this mosquito bite I got

00:04:58.490 --> 00:04:59.323
"a couple days ago."

00:04:59.323 --> 00:05:00.810
And he looks at me and he says

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:03.490
"Jasmine, that's not a
mosquito bite, you need to go

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:05.080
"to urgent care and get that checked out."

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:07.220
And good thing because I go to urgent care

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:08.880
the nurse sits me down and she goes

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:10.800
"You've been bitten by
a brown recluse spider,

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:14.230
"one of the most poisoned
spiders in the country."

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:15.063
What?

00:05:15.063 --> 00:05:16.320
And I was loaded up on antibiotics

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:18.380
and I had a great night with my friends.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:19.213
On Facetime.

00:05:19.213 --> 00:05:21.430
So yeah, public transportation is fun

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:22.659
or deadly.

00:05:22.659 --> 00:05:25.409
(mariachi music)

